{"kind":"assert","text":"Browser usability finding for the existing #18499 review: Hugh could not find review note #19016. Reproduced in actual native Chrome on main183211c3: the board Search requests query #190 shows #19012 but cannot return the standalone note #19016 in any request population. RequestList builds search candidates from commitment rows plus ratificationRows; awaitsRatification excludes render=note, so this note has no discoverable row. Its canonical #/thread/\u003cevent\u003e deep link does open #19016, proving it is present in the browser projection rather than lost or awaiting refresh. Expanding RecordDetail exposes text/body/bases and flags, but no evidence attachment list or links; the attached full review document therefore remains inaccessible through this detail view. Source inspection confirms RecordDetail has no attachment rendering. Include two small high-impact remedies in #18499's plan: exact event-number navigation/search that finds notes and other durable kinds while preserving clearly scoped request counts; and safe visible access to a record's attached evidence. Keep notes distinct from requests and approval duties; do not manufacture a request or adoption proposal solely to make a note visible. Immediate planner practice: provide verified deep links and a readable document link when sharing review notes. This finding adds concrete evidence to the already-assigned usability review, not a new implementation authorization.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:21b2806ed4f252e16193552b46606a10ae90eaa7 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:010aac64d68bdeac36cf6c443ce7305d53a60fe8, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:04075a23bf804a9e61f04055021af9a18d6ee9ca, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0453b72b3be2fd